        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Estrojam's Decibelle Music and Culture Festival\n- People: Wanda Jackson, Elvis Presley, Nina Hagen, Cat Power, Charlyn Marie \"Chan\" Marshall, Concrete Blonde, The Gossip, Peaches, Amy Ray, Margaret Cho\n- Organizations: Indigo Girls\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, musician, actress, model\n\nFacts:\n- Estrojam's Decibelle Music and Culture Festival previously featured Wanda Jackson, Nina Hagen, Concrete Blonde, Cat Power, The Gossip, Peaches, Amy Ray of the Indigo Girls, and Margaret Cho as headliners.\n- Wanda Jackson was known as the First Lady of Rock and toured with Elvis Presley in the 1950s and 1960s.\n- Charlyn Marie \"Chan\" Marshall was born on January 21, 1972.\n- Charlyn Marie \"Chan\" Marshall is better known by the stage name Cat Power.\n- Cat Power is an American singer-songwriter, musician, occasional actress, and model.",
